From 901ca0469f4ac6bcbd523dbc7c774b38e8e804a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adit <adit@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:44:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): vertical card layout on phones instead of a
 sideways-scrolling scene

Below 860px the diorama is cut into one framed card per station, stacked
vertically, each cropping the same drawing. Real full-size controls sit
underneath (tool chips, curve sliders with values, play button, hover/press
buttons, practice chips); the in-art copies become inert decoration so nothing
is duplicated for assistive tech. The controller sticks under the header and
chooses a card instead of dimming the others.
